# Property Assessment listing review

Public name: Property Assessment ("Kammer Report" is retired). The output is a call that can miss. No scores out of 100, no fight cards, no clickbait certainty. Popular is the input; judgment is the product. A #1 can still be a Pass, and Wait is a real call.

## Inputs
Address, ask, beds and baths, interior SF, neighbourhood, listing URL; the floor plan before the beauty shots; common charges and taxes; days on market, price history, same-building or nearby comps; price band on the weekly board ($5M to $10M, $10M to $15M, $15M to $20M); the RECORDS sweep.

## Process (same order every time)
1. One line: what they think they're buying.
2. Floor plan first: function.
3. One sentence per line:
   - WHO: one lifestyle it is unusually good for (never demographics).
   - USE: primary, family layout, pied-a-terre, entertaining or privacy.
   - FUNCTION: does the plan work in real life; only the 1 to 3 drivers that change the decision.
   - TRADE-OFF: what they give up.
   - MONEY: ask, SF, $/SF, comps, premium or discount, carry, price history; commodity floor plus trophy slice; name the scarcity in one noun; plus CARRY 5Y.
   - RISK: what a seduced buyer overrates, plus the RECORDS sweep.
   - RIVAL: the #2 in band, only if real.
   - EXIT: next-buyer pool, financeability, new supply, round-trip cost.
   - VERDICT: Pick, Consider, Wait or Pass, for that WHO.
4. One line: who it is wrong for.
5. Go deep on one hidden flaw until it is specific enough to be wrong later.
6. Wrinkle: one dry, highbrow line about the property (dead-room test). Never roast the buyer.
7. Stop. Fast on seven, deep on one.

## RECORDS sweep (fixed, about 15 minutes)
DOF tax bill (abatements and end dates), ACRIS (sale history, sponsor units, liens, declaration), DOB BIS / DOB NOW (C of O vs TCO, violations, FISP facade rating), HPD (complaints, violations), NYSCEF (suits naming board or sponsor), LL84 / LL97 (emissions, fine exposure), ZoLa (zoning, unused FAR next door, landmark district), FEMA and NYC flood maps, 311. Board minutes, financials, reserves and budgets are real-deal-only: say "unknown from public records", never guess. Every negative needs its source and date.

## CARRY 5Y
"Carry today $X. Heading up / flat / unknown, because ___." Drivers: abatement end, LL97 exposure, facade work, assessments, and the second-home surcharge only when USE is pied-a-terre.

## EXIT
Who buys it from you and how many exist at this price; financeability (litigation, or one owner or sponsor above 20% of units); sponsor still selling or new launches nearby; round-trip cost (mansion tax, transfer tax, flip tax). Note rendered or virtually staged photos.

## Light
Judge light from the plan, orientation of the main rooms, height versus neighbours and whether the view is protected or at risk (ZoLa, DOB NOW). Never narrate windows.

